id: pm-5ug5xq
title: Repository test runner inherits production Sentry and turns negative CLI fixtures into release-blocking incidents
description: "The canonical scripts/run-tests.mjs wrapper isolates PM_PATH and PM_GLOBAL_PATH but spreads the complete host environment into build, Vitest, and nested CLI subprocesses. On a developer host with production Sentry available, negative npm-package install fixtures emitted eight handled tar-extraction failures into the production project as PM-CLI-2G and PM-CLI-39 while the 2026.8.28 gate suite was running. The linked-test child boundary was fixed by pm-9aaji6, but the repository test entrypoint remains unguarded. The wrapper must disable external Sentry delivery by default for every child process without weakening explicit instrumentation unit tests, and repository governance must prevent the isolation contract from disappearing."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 0
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-28T16:48:05.770Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-28T17:48:58.174Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#143da6b99c6d50ff73f411da"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: "The canonical repository test wrapper forces external Sentry delivery off for build, Vitest, coverage, and nested CLI children even when the parent enables it; Instrumentation unit tests retain explicit mocked initialization coverage; A real npm registry package install succeeds through the validated SDK archive boundary; Focused tests, literal 100/100/100/100 full coverage, static quality, temporary-project acceptance, exact-head hosted checks, and bot review pass"
definition_of_ready: Live event timing and runtime metadata identify the local test runner; all-status duplicate search and the prior linked-child fix are recorded.
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make every canonical repository test execution observability-isolated and harden the SDK package archive boundary exposed by the incident.
value: Negative fixtures remain useful without corrupting production reliability signals or blocking releases.
impact: Restores trustworthy Sentry release gating and prevents registry tarballs from bypassing bounded archive validation.
outcome: Repository tests cannot emit production Sentry events; npm registry archives share local archive safety checks and typed missing-artifact recovery.
why_now: The v2026.8.28 release is blocked before publication by eight false production events from the canonical test run.
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: Local Ubuntu developer host running canonical repository gates with production Sentry credentials present; SDK npm package source resolution
repro_steps: Run node scripts/run-tests.mjs coverage on a host with production Sentry enabled while negative npm-package fixtures execute; observe handled missing-tar errors classified as production.
expected_result: Test failures remain local; registry archives are validated before extraction; missing npm pack artifacts return a stable path-redacted refusal.
actual_result: "The outer wrapper inherited production observability settings and the registry resolver called system tar directly, producing raw handled failures and accepting link entries."
affected_version: 2026.8.27
fixed_version: 2026.8.28
component: test harness / SDK extension package source resolver / release observability
regression: true
customer_impact: "No broken artifact was published, but the daily release was blocked and production diagnostics were polluted by local negative fixtures."
