comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T16:48:05.770Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-28: all-status searches for test Sentry isolation, production Sentry test events, tar extraction npm package Sentry, and run-tests environment isolation found the closed linked-child owner pm-9aaji6 and the broader open host-fault taxonomy pm-3lhth4, but no item owns the repository test wrapper. Live privacy-safe evidence: PM-CLI-2G has two new events and PM-CLI-39 has six events from 12:12:07Z through 12:12:27Z, all handled, environment=production, release=2026.8.27, Node 26.5.0 on the local Ubuntu kernel, with the expected missing tar archive negative-fixture error. No event ids, paths, host identities, or credentials are retained in PM."
  "2026-08-28T16:48:42.262Z","harness:codex","TDD red evidence: set PM_SENTRY_DISABLED=0 in the parent and required the canonical wrapper to force 1 in its child environment. The focused run failed exactly at that boundary: child inherited 0 instead of 1; 16 sibling tests passed. No production code changed before this negative control."
  "2026-08-28T17:15:13.610Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: scripts/run-tests.mjs now forces PM_SENTRY_DISABLED=1 after spreading the parent environment, so build, Vitest, and nested CLI children cannot deliver test failures externally even when the launching host sets PM_SENTRY_DISABLED=0. The real focused child regression passes 17/17, while Sentry instrumentation suites still pass through their mocked boundary. Two complete coverage runs created no new PM-CLI-2G or PM-CLI-39 events; their lastSeen values remain 12:12:27Z and 12:12:21Z with counts 5 and 6."
  "2026-08-28T17:36:24.026Z","harness:codex","Final local gate evidence before review: an additional TDD negative control proved npm's reported archive filename could escape the isolated pack destination; the test failed by resolving an absolute outside archive, then passed after adding the path-redacted npm_package_archive_unsafe refusal. Generated error catalogs, contracts, SDK surface, and refusal census are current. Full coverage passed 585 files / 8,089 tests at literal 100/100/100/100 (60,001 statements, 45,202 branches, 12,477 functions, 57,780 lines). The complete quality:static chain passed on final source, including build, contracts, type/doc coverage, ESLint, zero-duplicate jscpd, repository assurance, SDK/package/grammar/refusal/token/performance, graph-composition, and record-integrity gates. Security scan found no tracked credentials; pnpm audit found zero vulnerabilities; npm dry pack and deep package doctor passed. Temporary-project npm:pm-changelog 2026.8.22 install/activation and deep doctor passed with zero warnings/errors."
  "2026-08-28T17:48:58.174Z","harness:codex","Review-loop evidence for PR #1141: CodeRabbit reported no actionable code finding but warned that its diff-scoped docstring heuristic saw 0% on three changed private helpers. Added substantive behavior and invariant contracts to the canonical test runner, npm pack parser, and injectable registry resolver. Focused 28/28 regressions, targeted ESLint, and the six-assertion repository static-quality assurance gate pass after the change."
